{
  "about": "Shared by scripts/render-art.py (bakes the lens and the lights), src/components/Art.tsx (draws Ambience and the light layers) and scripts/check-contrast.py (gates the text). Amplitudes are in dp. A light's box is 'frame' (fills the screen frame) or {w,h} in units of the frame width, centred on the frame unless anchor is 'top'. Motion, for a linear clock p in 0..1 per period: orbit: the box centre sits on a circle of radius*frameWidth around the frame centre at angle phase + dir*360*p degrees; sway: translateX = dx*sin(2*pi*p), rotate = rotate*sin(2*pi*p) degrees; drift: translateX = ax*sin(2*pi*p), translateY = -ay*cos(2*pi*p), scale = 1 + s*sin(2*pi*p); slide: translateX = x0 - ax*sin(2*pi*p). header: the mountain art at the top of the Today trail; ratio is its height over its width. bounds: the part of a light's box where its alpha is visible at all (alpha > 0.004), as [x0, y0, x1, y1] fractions of the box; glass skips drawing a light whose bounds miss it.",
